# Layout port verification pin.
#
# This file names the Taffy revision the port tracks. `.references/taffy` is the
# authoritative source; update deliberately and re-run every gate below.
TAFFY_REPO="https://github.com/DioxusLabs/taffy.git"

# Tracked revision.
#
# Upstream main after v0.15.1 (2026-10-31). Every behavioural commit since the
# previous pin (22f941e) is ported; see docs/report.md.
TAFFY_REV="c6421c1cb20df5845e83285d3ce63c716f52186c" //gonna have to change this to the latest since i just did i git pull

# Baseline revision the port started from.
#
# Retained for regression comparison only: it is the pre-existing gate, not the
# behaviour the port targets. Two categories of fixture in that corpus cannot be
# satisfied by an implementation that tracks TAFFY_REV:
#
#   * Fixtures that omit `position`. Taffy's runner reads a missing `position` as
#     `Position::default()`, which became `Static` upstream; this corpus was
#     generated when the default was `Relative`. The runner exposes
#     `--default-position` to select the historical default so the baseline stays
#     runnable. See tools/fixtures/main.zig.
#
#   * Fixtures whose expected values upstream intentionally changed (rounding in
#     cumulative coordinates, percentage padding/border bases, margin
#     collapse-through, absolute auto margins, root insets, column intrinsic
#     sizing). Those expectations are correct for the old revision and wrong for
#     this one.
#
# To reconstruct it without touching `.references/taffy`:
#   mkdir -p /tmp/zafi-audit-pin/.references/taffy
#   git -C .references/taffy archive 1b918bafcab101dd234ebeb27da0443e24fd9de2 \
#     | tar -x -C /tmp/zafi-audit-pin/.references/taffy
TAFFY_BASELINE_REV="1b918bafcab101dd234ebeb27da0443e24fd9de2"

# Gates, in order. All must pass before a change is considered complete:
#
#   zig build test                    unit tests (Debug)
#   zig build test -Dserde=true       serde compatibility tests
#   zig build fixtures                TAFFY_REV XML corpus, all groups
#   (baseline corpus, informational, see above:
#      <fixtures-bin> --default-position relative)
#   zig build parity                  Rust-vs-Zig differential scenarios
#
# Performance gates are separate and are not correctness gates; see
# tools/bench/README.md for what each harness measures and does not.
